  "Id": 1242,
  "Title": "ISMC on the Future of Islamic Archaeology in Egypt",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Dr Stéphane Pradines speaking on the future of Islamic archaeology in Egypt.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass3CA159222EEC49BF9C3CF21EC81F26C3\"><p>Stéphane Pradines, ISMC associate&#160;professor, was invited by the French Institute of Archaeology in Cairo (IFAO) to participate in a debate on the future of Islamic archaeology in Egypt.&#160;<br></p><div>The seminar was organised by Marie-Odile Rousset (CNRS, Lyon) and Nicolas Michel (Director of the Arab Studies, IFAO).<br><br></div><div>His presentation included the results of 17 years of research in Fatimid Cairo, exposing the problems that he and his team faced in organising salvage and rescue excavations in a large city.&#160;</div><div><br></div><div>He also presented the positive inputs of his field school of Islamic archaeology, the biggest field school for the medieval period organised in Egypt and the Middle East.</div><div><br></div></div>",
